# The Hearth Store's daily look for updates (docs/HEARTH-STORE.md, "Finding updates"): a few small requests (each
# app's newest release on GitHub and its SHA256SUMS.txt; the signed list from hearthos.fun when Hearth OS has the
# owner's key), and one notice per new version when "Tell me when an update is ready" is on. It does nothing while a
# game runs, on a metered connection, or when Store settings says "Only when the Store opens". It downloads no app and
# writes only the Store's cache (~/.cache/hearth/store). Never touches booting, the system or the session.
[Unit]
Description=Hearth Store: look for updates (once a day)
ConditionPathExists=/usr/bin/hearth-store-app

[Service]
Type=oneshot
ExecStart=/usr/bin/hearth-store-app --check
TimeoutStartSec=3min
Nice=10
IOSchedulingClass=idle
